      <div type="clause" n="66.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 66.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="66.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa amansodne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.16"/> man oððe utlahne hæbbe ⁊ healde, plihte him sylfum ⁊ ealre his are.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="66.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hwa amansodne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.5"/> man oððon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.6"/> utlagene hæbbe ⁊ healde, plihte him sylfum ⁊ ealre his are.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="66.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="352" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa amansodne oððe utlahne habbe ⁊ healde, plihte him sylfum ⁊ ealre his are.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="66.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis excommunicatum uel utlagam habeat et manuteneat, dispereat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.25"/> idem et omnis eius uenia (desperatio sibi et omni [quę<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.26"/> possidet] uenię suę).</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="66.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis secum tenuerit excommunicatum aut exulem clamatum, careat omnibus bonis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.10"/> suis et uita, nisi ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.11"/> rex parcat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="66.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis excommunicatum tenet et seruat, caueat sibimet et uniuerse substantie sue.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="66.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="206" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf hwa amansodne<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_66-1.robnote.fn.9"/> man oððon utlagene hæbbe ⁊ healde, plihte him sylfum ⁊ ealre his are.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="286" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa amansodne man oððe utlahne hæbbe and healde, plihte him sylfum and ealre his are.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="353" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.de.1"/> einer einen excommunicirten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.de.2"/> Menschen oder einen friedlosen bei sich hat und unterhält, so bringe er seinem Leben und seiner ganzen Besitzerstellung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_66-1.lnote.de.3"/> Gefahr [der Verwirkung].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone keeps with him and maintains an excommunicated person or an outlaw, let him bring danger [of forfeiture] upon his life and his whole standing in property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_66-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="207" ed="#robertson"/>If anyone keeps and maintains an excommunicated man or an outlaw, it shall be at the risk of losing his life and all his property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_66-1.whinote.n.6"/><pb n="471" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone maintains and keeps an excommunicated person or an outlaw, let him be put in peril of his life and all his property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="287" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone shelters and supports an excommunicated person or an outlaw, it shall be at the risk of his life and all his property.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="353"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_42">VIII Atr 42</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VIII Atr. 42</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="471"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_42">VIII Atr 42</ref> <quote>cf. VIII Ethelred, 42</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 42.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 353, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät geänd.</hi> amansumodne [<hi rend="italic">archaisirend</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">late altered to amansumodne [archaizing]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert</hi> oððe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to oððe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dis. — uenia <hi rend="italic">KHn;</hi> des. — suę <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dis. — uenia KHn; des. — suę the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q. p. u. s. <hi rend="italic">nur Dm; nur</hi> u. s. [<hi rend="italic">frühere Form</hi>] <hi rend="italic">R; nur</hi> q. p. [<hi rend="italic">gebesserte Form</hi>] <hi rend="italic">THk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q. p. u. s. only Dm; only u. s. [earlier form] R; only q. p. [improved form] THk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">amers. <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">amers. without man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">rex ei <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">rex ei Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">In Widerspruch mit <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 13, 2 und 66¹·².—Benutzt durch Hn 11, 14. 13, 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In contradiction with <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 13, 2 and 66¹·².—Used by Hn 11, 14. 13, 10</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">In Widerspruch mit <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 13, 2 und 66¹·².—Benutzt durch Hn 11, 14. 13, 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In contradiction with <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 13, 2 and 66¹·².—Used by Hn 11, 14. 13, 10</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_66-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu Q's <hi rend="italic">venia vgl. o</hi>. 49⁴</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On Q’s <hi rend="italic">venia cf. above</hi> 49⁴</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_66-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VIII Atr. 42.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_66-1.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope></bibl><label>amansodne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Altered later to <hi rend="italic">amansumodne</hi> in B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_66-1.whinote.n.6" n="6" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">471</biblScope></bibl><label>66.1</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">cf. VIII Ethelred, 42</seg></note>
      </div>
